      "side": 1,
      "message": "While `sk_sp\u003cconst Foo\u003e` or any `const Foo` where `Foo : public SkRefCnt` is fine but should always be redundant, which is why we often don\u0027t. That is to say, if a class has an intrusive thread safe reference count it should already by externally const to be thread safe. So, yeah, `const` here is correct, it\u0027s just annoying that the default is mutable so `const` is all noisy and in one\u0027s face.\n\nThat being said, `SkData` does have non-const methods for construction purposes, so this might be fine.\n\nIf this is a crusade to make as many `sk_sp\u003cFoo\u003e` into `sk_sp\u003cconst Foo\u003e` as possible, that\u0027s fine, just wanted to note that this wasn\u0027t already the case due to the visual noise of the extra `const` (which should be implicit) when the classes should always be logically const anyway after construction / initialization (before the first additional reference escapes).",
